  "notes": "{違法|いほう} indicates something that violates the law. It functions as both a noun and a na-adjective: {違法|いほう}な{行為|こうい} (an illegal act), {違法|いほう}だ (it is illegal).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {違法|いほう}{駐車|ちゅうしゃ}: illegal parking\n- {違法|いほう}{行為|こうい}: illegal act\n- {違法|いほう}{改造|かいぞう}: illegal modification\n- {違法|いほう}コピー: illegal copy, piracy\n- {違法|いほう}{薬物|やくぶつ}: illegal drugs\n- {違法|いほう}に: illegally (adverbial)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {合法|ごうほう}: legal, lawful (direct opposite)\n- {不法|ふほう}: unlawful, illegal (similar meaning, often used in {不法|ふほう}{侵入|しんにゅう} \"trespassing\")\n\nREGISTER:\nFormal. Common in legal, news, and official contexts.",
